From 7a11cf95a2a110bf80d9943e27048b847999f141 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Freddie Honohan <honohanf@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 22:16:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] Spend: operand ranges, OP_VER, strict signature / key
 encoding and minimal pushes as ts-sdk Spend has them

- OP_PICK / OP_ROLL / OP_SPLIT / OP_NUM2BIN: an operand too large for an i64 was read as 0; it now fails the
  range check, as in ts-sdk. OP_LSHIFT / OP_RSHIFT: a count past every bit gives zeros of the input's width.
- OP_VER pushes the tx version as 4 little-endian bytes (node v1.2.0), not as a script number.
- CHECKSIG / CHECKMULTISIG: a malformed signature (strict DER, defined hash type, Chronicle bit only when
  relaxed, low S under the version-1 policy) or public key is an error, not a false result.
- Under the version-1 policy an executed data push must be minimally encoded.

Found by b017-native's interpreter differential; all 20000 random scripts now agree with ts-sdk.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
